# Settings section cards (tinted containers)

When a settings modal, floating panel, or multi-group form shows **several independent concerns**, wrap each concern in its own **tinted section card**. Adjacent cards must use **different tones** so groups are easy to scan (보기 설정 / 문서 설정 pattern).

## Shared helper

Use `settingsSectionCardClass` from `src/utils/settingsSectionCard.ts` — do not invent one-off border/bg strings.

```tsx
import { settingsSectionCardClass } from '@/utils/settingsSectionCard';

<div className="flex flex-col gap-2.5 p-3"> {/* or space-y-3 in a modal body */}
  <section className={settingsSectionCardClass('sky')} aria-label="…">
    {/* one concern */}
  </section>
  <section className={settingsSectionCardClass('violet')} aria-label="…">
    {/* another concern */}
  </section>
  <section className={settingsSectionCardClass('emerald')} aria-label="…">
    …
  </section>
</div>
```

Compact floating panels: `settingsSectionCardClass('sky', { compact: true })`.

Tone rotation when stacking many sections: `SETTINGS_SECTION_TONE_SEQUENCE` (`sky` → `violet` → `amber` → `emerald` → `blue` → `slate`).

## Checklist

1. One card = one concern (do not dump the whole form into a single tint).
2. Neighboring cards use **different** tones — never identical tint back-to-back.
3. Prefer the helper over raw Tailwind color stacks.
4. Keep modal sticky header/footer outside the scroll body; cards live **inside** the scrolling body only.
5. Nested lists/inputs inside a card may use a slightly stronger surface (`bg-white/80`) for contrast.
6. Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

```text
❌ BAD — flat sections with only headings, no card chrome
❌ BAD — every section the same slate/gray card (no hue separation)
❌ BAD — hand-rolled border-sky-… strings when the helper exists
✅ GOOD — settingsSectionCardClass + distinct tones per section
✅ GOOD — DocumentSettingsModal / HaimProseWidthFloatingPanel (보기 설정)
```
